-- title:
--   A compactly supported window for the local weighted discrepancy
-- statement:
--   Let $L/K$ be an extension of number fields that is finite and Galois, let $\sigma \in \mathrm{Gal}(L/K)$ be such that every element of the group lies in the subgroup generated by $\sigma$, and let $\ell = [L:K]$ be prime. Fix a nonzero prime $v$ of $\mathcal{O}_K$, a function $\varphi$ on $\mathrm{GL}_2(L \otimes_K K_v)$ that is locally constant with compact support, a function $f$ on $\mathrm{GL}_2(K_v)$ that is locally constant with compact support, and assume $\varphi$ and $f$ match locally in the sense of [`AutomorphicForm.AreMatchingLocal`](def/AutomorphicForm_TwistedOrbital.html#L386): with respect to the Haar measures on $\mathrm{GL}_2(L\otimes_K K_v)$ and $\mathrm{GL}_2(K_v)$ normalised by the integral sets, every twisted orbital integral of $\varphi$ at a $\delta$ whose norm string is regular semisimple agrees with the orbital integral of $f$ at any regular semisimple $\gamma$ admitting a norm conjugator to $\delta$, for coupled Haar measures on the twisted centraliser and the centraliser; and the orbital integral of $f$ at a regular semisimple $\gamma$ that is not a norm vanishes. Then there is a function $\Psi$ on $K_v^\times \times K_v^\times$ with the following four properties. First, $\Psi$ has compact support. Second, $\Psi$ is locally constant away from $t = 1$: for every $p$ with second coordinate $\neq 1$ there is a neighbourhood of $p$ on which $\Psi$ takes the value $\Psi(p)$. Third, there is a constant $C$ with $\|\Psi(a,t) - \Psi(a,1)\| \le C\,\|1-t\|\,(1 + |\log\|1-t\||)$ for all $a, t \in K_v^\times$. Fourth, for all $a, t \in K_v^\times$ with $t \ne 1$, put $\gamma = \mathrm{diag}(a, at)$, and let $\tau$ be any Haar measure on the centraliser of $\gamma$ in $\mathrm{GL}_2(K_v)$ (with its Borel structure) giving mass $1$ to the set of elements of the centraliser lying in [`AutomorphicForm.localIntegralSet`](def/AutomorphicForm_LocalOrbitalBase.html#L100), that is, with the element and its inverse having entries in $\mathcal{O}_v$; and let $J \in \mathbb{C}$ be any weighted orbital integral of $f$ at $\gamma$ relative to $\tau$, namely $J = \int f(x^{-1}\gamma x)\,w(x)\,s(x)\,d\mu$ for some section function $s$, with $w$ the local weight. Then, writing $r = \|1 - t\| \cdot \sqrt{\|a\|/\|at\|}$, two clauses hold: (i) for all units $\alpha,\beta$ of $L \otimes_K K_v$ such that the norm string $\prod_{i<\ell}\sigma^i(\mathrm{diag}(\alpha,\beta))$ equals the image of $\gamma$ under $\mathrm{GL}_2(K_v) \to \mathrm{GL}_2(L\otimes_K K_v)$, for every Haar measure $\tau'$ on the $\sigma$-twisted centraliser $\{x : x\,\delta\,\sigma(x)^{-1} = \delta\}$ of $\delta = \mathrm{diag}(\alpha,\beta)$ giving mass $1$ to the semi-local integral set, and every $J'$ that is a twisted weighted orbital integral of $\varphi$ at $\delta$ relative to $\tau'$, one has $r\,(J' - \ell J) = \Psi(a,t)$; and (ii) if no such $\alpha,\beta$ exist, then $r\,(0 - \ell J) = \Psi(a,t)$.
--
--   This is the local window at a finite place in the cyclic prime-degree base-change comparison: the normalised difference between the twisted weighted orbital integral of a semi-local test function and $\ell$ times the weighted orbital integral of a matching local test function is realised by a single compactly supported function of the split torus parameters, locally constant away from the singular locus $t=1$ and with a logarithmic-rate germ there. In this form it is consumed by the assembly of the global class-sum window identities, both in the unweighted form and in the variant where the normalising factor $\|1-t\|\sqrt{\|a\|/\|at\|}$ is inverted.
